{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וישא משלו", :translit "vayisa meshalo", :gloss "and he took up his parable"} {:he "מברך רעהו בקול גדול", :translit "mevareich re'ehu be-kol gadol", :gloss "blesses his neighbor with a loud voice"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Proverbs 26:24 read as a warning: a loud blessing may mask a curse."}], :frame {:text "Proverbs 27:14 states: 'He who blesses his neighbor with a loud voice, rising early in the morning, it shall be counted a curse to him.' Ba'al HaTurim applies this verse to Balaam, who raised his voice so all seventy nations would hear and yet his words were reckoned as curses rather than blessings.", :sources ["Proverbs 27:14"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מן ארם", :translit "min aram", :gloss "from Aram"} {:he "לך לך מארצך", :translit "lekh lekha me-artzekha", :gloss "go for yourself from your land"} {:he "ואברכך", :translit "va-avarekhekha", :gloss "and I will bless you"} {:he "והנה אנכי עמך ושמרתיך", :translit "ve-hineh anokhi imkha ve-shmartikha", :gloss "and behold I am with you and I will guard you"} {:he "הנה ילדה מלכה גם היא", :translit "hineh yaldah milkhah gam hi", :gloss "behold Milcah too has borne"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Two interpretations linking Aram to Abraham's and Jacob's blessings and to the intertwined origins of Israel and Moab."}], :frame {:text "Genesis 12:1–2 records God's call to Abraham to leave Aram/Nahor accompanied by the promise 'I will bless you.' Genesis 28:15 records the parallel blessing given to Jacob on his journey to Aram: 'And behold I am with you and I will guard you.' Genesis 22:20–21 records that 'after these things' — immediately following the Akeidah — news arrived that 'Milcah too has borne' children to Nahor in Aram. Ba'al HaTurim weaves these together: Balak hails from that same Aram and yet comes to curse the descendants of those who left Aram laden with blessings. The frame rests entirely on these verse addresses.", :sources ["Genesis 12:1" "Genesis 12:2" "Genesis 28:15" "Genesis 22:20" "Genesis 22:21"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מן ארם", :translit "min aram", :gloss "from Aram"} {:he "אשל", :translit "eshel", :gloss "terebinth / inn"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "מן ארם", :b "אשל"}], :frame {:text "Genesis 21:33 states: 'And Abraham planted an eshel in Be'er Sheva and there he called upon the name of the Lord.' The gematria equating 'from Aram' with 'eshel' links Balaam's Aramean origin to the merit Abraham acquired through planting the eshel.", :sources ["Genesis 21:33"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ינחני", :translit "yenakhneini", :gloss "He leads me"} {:he "ינחני בלק", :translit "yenakhneini balak", :gloss "Balak leads me"} {:he "ינחני במעגלי צדק", :translit "yenakhneimi be-ma'aglei tzedek", :gloss "He leads me in circles of justice"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ינחני בלק" "ינחני במעגלי צדק"]}], :frame {:text "Psalm 23:3 states 'He leads me in circles of justice for His name's sake.' Ba'al HaTurim links the two occurrences of the lemma ינחני, reading the verse as a description of how God redirected Balak's attempt to curse Israel into a path of justice.", :sources ["Psalm 23:3"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ינחני", :translit "yenakhneini", :gloss "He leads me"} {:he "לגיהנם", :translit "le-gehinnom", :gloss "to Gehenna"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ינחני", :b "לגיהנם"}], :frame nil} {:quotes [{:he "מהררי קדם", :translit "me-harerei kedem", :gloss "from the mountains of the east"} {:he "אם אני לא אעבור", :translit "im ani lo e'evor", :gloss "if I do not pass"} {:he "הגל הזה", :translit "ha-gal ha-zeh", :gloss "this cairn"} {:he "ההרים רקדו כאילים", :translit "he-harim rakdu ke-eylim", :gloss "the mountains skipped like rams"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Two interpretations: the covenant at the cairn of Genesis 31, and the mountains' praise at Sinai in Psalm 114."}], :frame {:text "Genesis 31:51–52 records that Jacob and Laban set up a cairn (גל) as a boundary witness and declared 'If I do not pass this cairn to you.' Psalm 114:4 describes the revelation at Sinai: 'The mountains skipped like rams.' Ba'al HaTurim reads both as reasons Balaam could not curse Israel — a covenantal boundary and the mountains' act of honor at Sinai.", :sources ["Genesis 31:51" "Genesis 31:52" "Psalm 114:4"]}} {:quotes [{:he "מהררי קדם", :translit "me-harerei kedem", :gloss "from the mountains of the east"} {:he "מאבות העולם", :translit "me-avot ha-olam", :gloss "from the fathers of the world"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "מהררי קדם", :b "מאבות העולם"}], :frame nil} {:quotes [{:he "ארה לי יעקב ולכה זועמה ישראל", :translit "arah li ya'akov u-lakhah zo'ehmah yisra'el", :gloss "How shall I curse Jacob and how shall I denounce Israel"} {:he "ובאו עליך כל הקללות", :translit "u-va'u kha kol ha-kelalot", :gloss "and all the curses shall come upon you"} {:he "יצו ה' אתך את הברכה", :translit "yitzaveh Hashem itekha et ha-berakhah", :gloss "the Lord will set upon you the blessing"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Contrast: curses in Deut 28 lack God's name; blessings in Deut 28 carry the Tetragrammaton."}], :frame {:text "Genesis 28:3 records Isaac blessing Jacob by the name Jacob. Genesis 35:10 records that God renamed him Israel. Deuteronomy 28:2 introduces the blessing with the Tetragrammaton — 'YHWH will set upon you the blessing' — while the curse passage in Deuteronomy 28:15 says only 'all these curses shall come upon you' without invoking God's name directly. Ba'al HaTurim sees both details as barring Balaam from cursing under either name.", :sources ["Genesis 28:3" "Genesis 35:10" "Deuteronomy 28:2" "Deuteronomy 28:15"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Proverbs 26:24 read as a warning: a loud blessing may mask a curse.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Two interpretations linking Aram to Abraham's and Jacob's blessings and to the intertwined origins of Israel and Moab.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "מן ארם", :a-value 331, :b "אשל", :b-value 331, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ינחני בלק" "ינחני במעגלי צדק"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ינחני בלק", :refs ["Numbers 23:7"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ינחני במעגלי צדק", :refs ["Psalms 23:3"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :gematria, :a "ינחני", :a-value 128, :b "לגיהנם", :b-value 138, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :other, :note "Two interpretations: the covenant at the cairn of Genesis 31, and the mountains' praise at Sinai in Psalm 114.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:a-value 599, :b-value 600, :lens :standard, :equal? false, :kind :gematria, :b "מאבות העולם", :by :selah, :colel? true, :a "מהררי קדם"} {:kind :other, :note "Contrast: curses in Deut 28 lack God's name; blessings in Deut 28 carry the Tetragrammaton.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:31:17.228474709Z", :model "glm-5.2"}